SUMMARY:Lunchtime Discovery: From Mountains to Sea at the Cameron Art Museum
DESCRIPTION:Join us in-person in the SECU Daily Planet Theater or watch the livestream on YouTube. \nThe From Mountains to Sea exhibit explores the evolving relationship between humanity and the natural world. Each artwork is more than an image – it forms part of an ongoing dialogue with the land we call home\, from the coastal plain to the mountain communities recently reshaped by Hurricane Helene. Discover how contemporary North Carolina artists convey the complex connections between people and their environment. \nSeptember Krueger\, Curator of Education and Public Programs\, Cameron Art Museum\nBen Billingsley\, Associate Curator\, Cameron Art Museum \n\nThroughout the month of April\, the Lunchtime Discovery Series will recognize Earth Day. These live presentations will be held Wednesdays from noon to 1:00 p.m. and are hosted by the NC Museum of Natural Sciences Coordinator of Current Science Programs Chris Smith. \nBrought to you by the NC DEQ Office of Environmental Education and Public Affairs and the NC Museum of Natural Sciences.
URL:https://naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/lunchtime-discovery-from-mountains-to-sea-at-the-cameron-art-museum-2/
LOCATION:Nature Research Center\, 121 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
